From dd93c06cd4a03367b15744b00a041f73c7a36498 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 19:57:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show the owner's real reference photo as the example, not a
 cartoon diagram
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The photo-review screen shown after every single shot (retake or use this
photo?) always rendered the generic SVG car-shape illustration as the
"EXAMPLE" column, even when the owner had already uploaded a real reference
photo for that exact angle — the one place a driver looks at most often
during capture was the one place still using the placeholder art.

- PhotoReviewModal now shows the owner's real reference photo when one
  exists for that shot, falling back to the SVG diagram only when it
  doesn't.
- The empty (not-yet-captured) shot tiles on the capture grid now show the
  reference photo directly as a dimmed background with a gold "REF" tag,
  instead of a plain dashed placeholder — so the example is visible before
  the driver even taps to open the camera, not hidden behind the info icon.
